From ae615a352272fe6876816907e4c61e3cf735bd55
Subject: bevy_scene: forget child instances with their parent; unregister cancels pending spawns
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/bevy/commit/ae615a352272fe6876816907e4c61e3cf735bd55
Date: 2026-09-25T16:54:16+01:00

`SceneSpawner` kept an instance's entity map until `despawn_instance`
or `unregister_instance` was called. Only the `SceneRoot` hooks do that
automatically, so instances spawned with `spawn_as_child` and then torn
down by despawning their parent (or their entities) stayed recorded for
the life of the app.

The parent of each child instance is now recorded, and
`scene_spawner_system` forgets spawned instances whose parent is gone,
alongside the loading instances it already dropped. `unregister_instance`
also removes an instance that has not spawned yet, so it never spawns.
